          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP293 – Val Quentin

Posted: N53 40.336 W114 23.105

My GPSr: N53 40.336 W114 23.10[b]6[/b]

My Elevation: 726 m&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I'd been here before and struck out, so this time I came with more tools, including a metal detector. With a previous context photo in mind, I made a quick recon of where I thought it might be and came up with nothing: the grass here is very lush and thick. So, I decided I'd bring out the “big guns” and find this guy. After two steps on the way back to the car, my foot hit something. What's this? The cap!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Now I have yet another tool in my cap hunting arsenal: just walk around and trip over things. I'll be sure to use it often, but only for the forces of good.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Thanks for the cap!&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
